WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.060
Rhiannon: Individuals who work with
children and young people play a crucial

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:08.200
role in shaping their lives and are
responsible for managing risks, using

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.440
the correct resources, establishing a
safe environment and safeguarding them

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.709
from harm or unprofessional conduct.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.230
Leah: Children and young people have
a right to be treated with respect

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:22.320
and dignity and It follows, that
trusted adults are expected to take

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.940
reasonable steps to ensure the safety
and well-being of children and young

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.290
people as part of that ‘duty of care’.

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:33.249
Rhiannon: All workplaces, whether a
school, a care provider or justice

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:38.180
service organisation have a moral and a
legal obligation to ensure that everyone

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.680
associated with that establishment,
whether employee, volunteer, student,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.480
tradesperson or the general public,
is fully protected from any personal

00:00:47.509 --> 00:00:51.740
physical or emotional harm, either
on the premises or when engaged in

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.870
activities relating to that establishment.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:58.030
Leah: Typical areas of concern are
fire safety, health and safety,

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:03.690
food safety, personal safety, child
and adult protection, safeguarding

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:10.750
such as safer recruitment, equality,
bullying, violence, harassment, stress,

00:01:10.809 --> 00:01:12.249
or discrimination from any source.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:22.789
Rhiannon: A breach of ‘duty of care’
occurs when a person or an organisation

00:01:23.059 --> 00:01:24.750
fails to live up to that standard.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:29.100
A person may be liable for negligence
in a personal injury case if their

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:32.929
breach of duty caused another person's
injuries or mental ill health.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:37.179
Leah: In education ‘duty of care’
is measured as being that of a

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:41.030
‘reasonable parent’ as when parents
leave their child at the school gates,

00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:44.560
they are in effect agreeing to allow
the teachers and other staff at the

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.569
school to act ‘in loco parentis’.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:51.530
Rhiannon: This means, that ‘in place of a
parent’, all teachers, including trainees,

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:56.070
have a 'duty of care' towards their pupils
and are required to apply their education

00:01:56.099 --> 00:01:58.720
and acquired skills to safeguard pupils.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:05.249
Leah: Any facilities need to be safe
and fit for purpose and all pupils

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:09.119
of all abilities have the right to
be protected from harm, especially

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:10.470
those who may be vulnerable.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.490
For example, if a school arranges
trips, there needs to be enough

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.890
help and support to keep all
children safe with all potential

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:18.889
risks assessed.

00:02:19.059 --> 00:02:22.610
Rhiannon: A care provider is expected
to be trustworthy, and act in

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.549
accordance with their code of practice.

00:02:25.039 --> 00:02:28.060
They should be up to date with
knowledge and skills and ensure that

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:33.069
service is provided safely, and records
up-to-date, accurate and confidential

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:37.079
except where the wider duty of care
or public interest might at risk.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:41.019
Leah: In the criminal justice system,
the aim is for every child to have a

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:45.800
safe and crime-free life and make a
positive contribution to society with a

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.400
focus on child first, offender second.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.010
Rhiannon: To maintain ‘duty of
care’ all inspectors should make

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:55.759
sure that youth justice services
meet statutory requirements, and

00:02:55.759 --> 00:02:57.210
no one is taken advantage of.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:00.810
Leah: All individuals working with
children and young people need

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:04.690
to understand and acknowledge the
responsibilities and trust inherent

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:08.269
in their role and do what a reasonable
person, with their training and

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.709
background, can be expected to
do, to maintain a duty of care.

